" ============================================================================
" NOT PORTED — recorded so you know these were decisions, not oversights
" ============================================================================
"
"   <leader>ol / <leader>om   Lazy / Mason — Settings > Plugins is the analogue
"   <leader>fh                highlight-group picker — colorscheme debug tool
"   <leader>ii                nerd-font icon picker — no equivalent
"   <leader>fm                markdown-scoped file picker — no scoped action
"   <localleader>nf / ng      ~/Cloud/Notes picker — add Notes as a content
"                             root and use a custom scope in Find in Path, or
"                             keep a second project window open on it
"   ga / gA                   mini.align — nothing in IdeaVim or IntelliJ
"   <leader>ib / <leader>it   comment rule / boxed title — use Live Templates
"   s / S / r / R             flash.nvim — `set sneak` gets you s{char}{char};
"                             treesitter select maps loosely to Opt+Up
"                             (EditorSelectWord)
"   markdown gj/gk/g0/g$      no ftplugin mechanism in IdeaVim
"   terminal-mode maps        IntelliJ's terminal is a tool window, not a buffer
"   <C-_>                     may not reach IdeaVim at all; <C-\> covers it
"   <leader>a* Claude Code    the JetBrains plugin's action IDs are unknown —
"                             run :actionlist claude and add them yourself
"   Godot (gdscript LSP,
"   <leader>ff filter,
"   :GodotDocs)               staying in Neovim
"
" ============================================================================
" VERIFY BEFORE TRUSTING
" ============================================================================
"
" In IntelliJ, run :actionlist <pattern> and confirm each of these resolves.
" A wrong action ID fails silently — no error, the key just does nothing.
"
"   :actionlist Goto          gd, gD, ]] , [[
"   :actionlist Rename        <leader>lr, <leader>cr
"   :actionlist Reformat      gw, <leader>lf
"   :actionlist Doc           K
"   :actionlist InlayHints    <leader>lh   ← least confident of the set
"   :actionlist Error         ]d, [d
"   :actionlist ChangeMarker  ]c, [c
"   :actionlist Rollback      <leader>ghr
"   :actionlist Tab           <Tab>, <S-Tab>, <C-c>
"   :actionlist Switcher      <leader>fb
"   :actionlist Scratch       <leader>.
"   :actionlist ToolWindow    <C-\>, <leader>oy, <leader>od, <leader>gg
"   :actionlist Replace       <leader>si   ← "Replace" is generic, check it
"   :actionlist claude        the whole <leader>a group
